Extend AnyNestedCondition:

```java
class EitherProperty extends AnyNestedCondition {
  EitherProperty() { super(ConfigurationPhase.REGISTER_BEAN); }
  @ConditionalOnProperty("app.feature.a") static class A {}
  @ConditionalOnProperty("app.feature.b") static class B {}
}

@Configuration
@Conditional(EitherProperty.class)
class FeatureConfig { }
```
AllNestedConditions and NoneNestedConditions cover AND and NOT.

Put @Validated on the root class and @Valid on the nested field; nested constraints are not cascaded without @Valid:

```java
@Validated
@ConfigurationProperties("app")
record AppProps(@Valid @NotNull Db db) {
  record Db(@NotBlank String url, @Min(1) int poolSize) {}
}
```

Register a FilterRegistrationBean with an order lower than Spring Security's (SecurityProperties.DEFAULT_FILTER_ORDER = -100):

```java
@Bean
FilterRegistrationBean<LoggingFilter> logging() {
  var reg = new FilterRegistrationBean<>(new LoggingFilter());
  reg.setOrder(SecurityProperties.DEFAULT_FILTER_ORDER - 1);
  return reg;
}
```
Wrap the request in ContentCachingRequestWrapper so the body can be read after the controller consumes it.

Return a StreamingResponseBody or a Resource:

```java
@GetMapping("/export")
ResponseEntity<StreamingResponseBody> export() {
  return ResponseEntity.ok()
    .header(HttpHeaders.CONTENT_DISPOSITION, "attachment; filename=export.csv")
    .body(out -> repo.streamAll().forEach(row -> write(out, row)));
}
```
StreamingResponseBody runs on an async executor; configure spring.mvc.async.request-timeout. If streaming from JPA, keep the transaction/connection open for the stream's lifetime.

Declare an interface with @GetExchange/@PostExchange and create a proxy:

```java
interface UserClient {
  @GetExchange("/users/{id}") User get(@PathVariable long id);
}

@Bean
UserClient userClient(RestClient.Builder b) {
  var rc = b.baseUrl("https://api.example.com").build();
  return HttpServiceProxyFactory.builderFor(RestClientAdapter.create(rc)).build().createClient(UserClient.class);
}
```
Boot 4 adds @ImportHttpServices to register such clients without the boilerplate.

Declare an interface or record and return it from a query method:

```java
record UserSummary(String name, String email) {}
List<UserSummary> findByActiveTrue();
```
Spring Data selects only the needed columns for closed projections. Open projections with @Value SpEL load the full entity, so prefer closed interfaces or DTO records.

For RestClient/RestTemplate use @RestClientTest with MockRestServiceServer:

```java
@RestClientTest(UserClient.class)
class UserClientTest {
  @Autowired UserClient client; @Autowired MockRestServiceServer server;
  @Test void handles500() {
    server.expect(requestTo("/users/1")).andRespond(withServerError());
    assertThatThrownBy(() -> client.get(1)).isInstanceOf(UpstreamException.class);
  }
}
```
Alternatively use WireMock for HTTP-level testing, which works with any client.

With @WebMvcTest, import your SecurityFilterChain config and use spring-security-test:

```java
@Test @WithMockUser(roles = "ADMIN")
void adminCanDelete() throws Exception {
  mvc.perform(delete("/users/1").with(csrf())).andExpect(status().isNoContent());
}
@Test void anonymousIsRejected() throws Exception {
  mvc.perform(delete("/users/1").with(csrf())).andExpect(status().isUnauthorized());
}
```
For JWT resource servers use .with(jwt().authorities(...)).

Declare two SecurityFilterChain beans with @Order and securityMatcher:

```java
@Bean @Order(1)
SecurityFilterChain api(HttpSecurity http) throws Exception {
  return http.securityMatcher("/api/**")
    .authorizeHttpRequests(a -> a.anyRequest().authenticated())
    .oauth2ResourceServer(o -> o.jwt(Customizer.withDefaults()))
    .sessionManagement(s -> s.sessionCreationPolicy(STATELESS))
    .csrf(c -> c.disable()).build();
}
@Bean @Order(2)
SecurityFilterChain web(HttpSecurity http) throws Exception {
  return http.authorizeHttpRequests(a -> a.anyRequest().authenticated())
    .formLogin(Customizer.withDefaults()).build();
}
```
The first chain whose matcher matches handles the request.

Keycloak puts roles in realm_access.roles, which the default converter (reads scope/scp) ignores. Register a JwtAuthenticationConverter with a custom authorities converter:

```java
@Bean
JwtAuthenticationConverter jwtConverter() {
  var c = new JwtAuthenticationConverter();
  c.setJwtGrantedAuthoritiesConverter(jwt -> ((List<String>) ((Map<String,Object>) jwt.getClaim("realm_access")).get("roles"))
    .stream().map(r -> new SimpleGrantedAuthority("ROLE_" + r)).collect(toList()));
  return c;
}
```

```java
@Bean @Order(1)
SecurityFilterChain actuator(HttpSecurity http) throws Exception {
  return http.securityMatcher(EndpointRequest.toAnyEndpoint())
    .authorizeHttpRequests(a -> a
      .requestMatchers(EndpointRequest.to(HealthEndpoint.class)).permitAll()
      .anyRequest().hasRole("ADMIN"))
    .httpBasic(Customizer.withDefaults()).build();
}
```
EndpointRequest follows management.endpoints.web.base-path and the management port automatically.

Implement InfoContributor:

```java
@Component
class FeatureInfo implements InfoContributor {
  public void contribute(Info.Builder b) { b.withDetail("features", Map.of("beta", true)); }
}
```
Built-in contributors: build (needs build-info), git (needs git.properties from git-commit-id plugin), env (management.info.env.enabled=true, info.* properties), java, os, process.

Native images include only reachable code; reflection targets must be declared. Register hints:

```java
@ImportRuntimeHints(MyHints.class)
class Config {}
class MyHints implements RuntimeHintsRegistrar {
  public void registerHints(RuntimeHints h, ClassLoader cl) {
    h.reflection().registerType(Foo.class, MemberCategory.values());
  }
}
```
Or use @RegisterReflectionForBinding(Foo.class). Run the app on the JVM with the native-image tracing agent to discover missing hints, and test with nativeTest.

Use ApplicationStartup:

```java
SpringApplication app = new SpringApplication(App.class);
app.setApplicationStartup(new BufferingApplicationStartup(2048));
app.run(args);
```
Then GET /actuator/startup lists steps (bean instantiation etc.) with durations. FlightRecorderApplicationStartup records the same into JFR.

Configure a DefaultErrorHandler with a DeadLetterPublishingRecoverer:

```java
@Bean
DefaultErrorHandler errorHandler(KafkaTemplate<Object,Object> t) {
  return new DefaultErrorHandler(new DeadLetterPublishingRecoverer(t), new FixedBackOff(1000L, 3));
}
```
Boot wires a single DefaultErrorHandler bean into the listener container factory. Mark non-retryable exceptions with addNotRetryableExceptions. For non-blocking retries with delay topics, use @RetryableTopic.

Use Resilience4j (resilience4j-spring-boot3 or Spring Cloud CircuitBreaker):

```java
@CircuitBreaker(name = "inventory", fallbackMethod = "fallback")
@Retry(name = "inventory")
Stock check(String sku) { return client.check(sku); }
```
Configure thresholds in resilience4j.circuitbreaker.instances.inventory.*. Retry wraps circuit breaker by default; make sure retried calls are idempotent. Spring Framework 7 also adds core @Retryable and @ConcurrencyLimit.
